«
@@ Cycling — turn a bounded interval into its next equivalent form:
@@ a…b → c±d → c±p% → a…b, keeping its unit. The three forms state
@@ the same bounds. A value a±σb is refused: a standard deviation is
@@ not a bound, and has no equivalent interval (see Bound→σ for the
@@ link between a bound and a standard deviation).
@@ Author & design          : Jean Wilson
@@ Co-authors & programming  : Claude & Claude Code (Anthropic)
  → cyx
  «
    @ The value without its unit, and the unit as 1_unit (or 1)
    1 cyx
    If cyx TypeName "unit" == Then Drop Drop 1 cyx →Unit cyx UVal End
    → cyu cyv
    «
      cyv TypeName
      → cyt
      «
        Case
          cyt "uncertain" == Then
            "Cycling: a±σb is a standard deviation, not a bound; it has no equivalent interval" DoError
          End
          cyt "range" == cyt "drange" == Or cyt "prange" == Or Then
            cyv Cycle
          End
          "Cycling: expects an interval a…b, a±b or a±p%" DoError
        End
        If cyu TypeName "unit" == Then cyu * End
      »
    »
  »
»
